"C" c3 e "G" dB G2 | "Am" A3 c "Em" BG E2 | "F" F3 A "C" GE c2 | "F" F2 "G" G2 "C" C4 ||
w: Fie, nay, pri-thee, John, Do not quar-rel, man! Lets be mer-ry and drink a-bout;
%
"C" cg gc "G" Bg gB | "Am" Af fA "Em" Ge eG | "F" Fd dF "C" Ec cE | "F" D2 "G" B2  "C"c4 ||
w: You're a rogue, you chea-ted me! I'll prove be-fore this com-pa-ny, I caren't a farth-ing, sir, for all you are so stout!
%
"C" ge ca "G" fd Bg | "Am" ec Af "Em" dB Ge | "F" cA Fd "C" BG Eg | "F" a2 "G" g>f "C" e4 |]
w: Sir, you lie! I scorned your word, or a-ny man that wears a sword! For all your huff, who cares a damn, and who cares for you?
