W: Fie, nay, prithee, John,
W: Do not quarrel, man!
W: Lets be merry and drink about;
W:
W: You're a rogue, you cheated me!
W: I'll prove before this company,
W: I caren't a farthing, sir,
W: for all you are so stout!
W:
W: Sir, you lie! I scorned your word,
W: or any man that wears a sword!
W: For all your huff, who cares a damn,
W: and who cares for you?
